            "href": "https://www.scb.se/HA0202-en",
            "label": "Statistics page",
            "type": "text/html"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": [
        "The survey on foreign trade in services is mainly constructed to ensure good reliability in estimates by type of service, without country breakdown. Trade in services by country is expected to be of better quality for countries with which Sweden has more extensive trade in services, while the level of uncertainty is greater for countries with lower trade values. For this reason, country-specific statistics are published only for those countries with which Sweden has a higher level of trade in services. This also means that countries previously included in the publication won’t be updated if they no longer rank among Sweden’s major trading partners in services.  \r\n  \r\nCollected data also includes values that have not been allocated by country. From 2013 these values are in larger extent than before allocated to specific countries. The values are allocated by country using country allocated data.  \r\n  \r\nThe United Kingdom withdrew from the European Union on 31 January 2020. The entire time-series has been updated to only contain the current 27 EU member countries. The country group EU27 thus does not include Great Britain.  \r\n  \r\nFor more information on the sources of uncertainty in the statistics, see the Quality report: [See section documentation](https://www.scb.se/HA0202-en)  \r\n  \r\nFor a detailed description of service items, see Clarification of service item under: [See section more information](https://www.scb.se/HA0202-en)",
        "X"
      ],
